Historical Theme: Art as Religious Instruction for Illiterate People
Historical Period: Romanesque Period (Middle Ages)
Artwork Inspiration: Tympanum of the West Portal of Sainte-Foy
Medium: Stone sculpture / architectural reliefVisual 
Prompt:Create a large Romanesque stone sculpture above the entrance of a medieval church. Show Jesus sitting in the center as the main figure, with angels and other people around him. On one side, show people going to heaven, and on the other side, show people facing punishment for their sins. Use rough stone textures, simple human shapes, and clear details. Make Jesus larger than the other figures to show his importance. Use natural stone colors and a balanced design.During the Middle Ages, many people could not read. Churches used these sculptures to teach people about Christianity, heaven, hell, and good and bad actions. The artwork helped people understand religious stories through pictures.
